 "result_text": "Fixed in `wcmatch/glob.py`. Putting a plain pattern before a magic one no longer breaks the magic pattern's results.\n\nThe cause was what the issue describes. A non-magic pattern like `dummy` overwrote `curdir`. A later magic pattern then started globbing from that stale directory instead of the starting directory. I changed the magic-pattern branch to always start globbing from the empty (current) directory.\n\nI checked it two ways, without adding any tests:\n- **Reordered patterns:** `glob(['**/setup.py', 'dummy'])` and the reversed list now give the same result.\n- **Mixed patterns:** `glob(['dummy', '*.toml'])` and `glob(['*.toml', 'dummy'])` both return `['pyproject.toml']`.\n\n`glob(['dummy', '**/*.toml'])` returned `[]`, but that was from a different directory than the other checks. I didn't look into that case further. I also didn't run the existing test suite.\n\nI left the `curdir = self.current` line at the top of `glob()` in place. It is now unused by the magic branch, so you could remove it as cleanup.",
